            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="0713" n="701" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg701"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.857/58: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-02-26T18:00:00-05:00">February 26,
                            1940—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. Your 68, February 22, 9 p.m. Please inform Aranha that the Department will
                    shortly express to the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Panama its agreement as to
                    the suitability of a collective protest against the violation of the security
                    zone resulting from the <hi rendition="#italic">Wakama</hi> incident, and its
                    acceptance of the text of the protest drafted by the Brazilian Government and
                    made available to the Department by the Brazilian Ambassador here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
